{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjqkBCxuSc16p691aTg1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VgpSvSn8NLhdoD1hHjFyXk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-061300__x488eb9/work/Sec*/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 14160,14216p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-260; sed -n 4017,4045p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"bindings\\|keys: 'right'\\|halves\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"E.Menu = \\|class Menu\" my-3d2dge.js; grep -n \"pointer()\\|clicked()\" my-3d2dge.js | head -5 | cut -c1-300","description":"Read Story manual, touch notice and player key halves"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8658,"cache_read_input_tokens":135079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8658},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4983f3c-8ab3-4cb5-bbfd-23a240d1dce6","uuid":"335138aa-9ccd-4575-b8e2-4bcd41cb27c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:14:07.416Z","request_id":"req_011CgjqkAuLw5XsFp51q27wV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VgpSvSn8NLhdoD1hHjFyXk":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-061300__x488eb9/work/Sec*/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 14160,14216p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-260; sed -n 4017,4045p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"bindings\\|keys: 'right'\\|halves\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"E.Menu = \\|class Menu\" my-3d2dge.js; grep -n \"pointer()\\|clicked()\" my-3d2dge.js | head -5 | cut -c1-300","description":"Read Story manual, touch notice and player key halves"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VgpSvSn8NLhdoD1hHjFyXk","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.89.1: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n```\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module STORY: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * STORY  conversations as data run through a Dialog, flags and values, quests, emote balloons\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { px } = E;\nconst HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RRRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a' });\nGame.prototype._needSync = function () {\n  const fine = window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches, coarse = window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\n  const need = coarse && !fine && !this._keyed && this.input.padIndex === null, el = this._needEl;\n  if (!need) { if (el) el.style.display = 'none'; return; }\n  if (!el) {\n    const d = this._needEl = document.createElement('div'); d.setAttribute('data-sys', 'need'); d.setAttribute('role', 'alert');\n    d.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.88);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\n    d.innerHTML = '<div><div style=\"font-size:21px;margin-bottom:8px\">Controller or keyboard required</div><div style=\"opacity:.8;margin-bottom:18px\">This game plays with a controller or a keyboard. Connect one, then press any button.</div><button type=\"button\" style=\"font:inherit;padding:10px 22px;border-radius:10px;border:2px solid #b8a8ff;background:#2a2050;color:#fff;min-width:44px;min-height:\n    d.querySelector('button').onclick = () => this.menu('settings');\n    (this.screen.canvas.parentElement || document.body).appendChild(d);\n  }\n  this._needEl.style.display = this.shell && this.shell.screen ? 'none' : 'flex';   // (Settings open over it: hidden while it is)\n};\n/* =============================================================================\n * 11. HUMANOID RIG\n *    Local frame: f = forward, r = right, z = up. The rig poses itself every step\n *    from movement, attacks and state, then projects through any view.\n *    Attack specs (angles relative to facing, + = toward the right hand):\n *      { a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, blade, spin }   e.g. horizontal slash a0: 1.7 -> a1: -1.9\n *    Drive with rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack:{ spec, phase, u } })\n *    where phase is 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover' and u is 0..1 progress in that phase.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst HUMAN_COLORS = {\n  skin: '#f1c7a0', hair: '#3b2a2f', cloth: '#2f8f86', pants: '#3b3552', boot: '#6a4128', belt: '#e0a84a',\n  cape: '#c8452f', capeIn: '#7a2622', metal: '#dce8f1', metalDk: '#7f93ab', hilt: '#e8b04e', eye: '#1a1320'\n};\nconst JOINT_KEYS = ['hipL', 'hipR', 'kneeL', 'kneeR', 'footL', 'footR', 'hipC', 'shC', 'shL', 'shR', 'head', 'elbowL', 'elbowR', 'handL', 'handR'];\n/** body proportions: 'chibi' (default, big head, Secret of Mana), 'heroic' (tall, Symphony of the Night), 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) */\nconst BUILDS = {\n792:     *  0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's two halves, a rhythm game's lanes. A finger\n807:     *  game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them) */\n863:  /** switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings\n864:   *  (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER,\n869:    const B = this.bindings || {};\n874:      if (!Array.isArray(map[a])) continue;   // (a preset's halves: Input.halfKeys)\n894:  /** the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them) */\n895:  get bindings() { return this._bindings || {}; }\n896:  set bindings(b) { this._bindings = b && typeof b === 'object' ? b : {}; if (this.preset) this.use(this.preset); }\n907:    this._setBindings(Object.assign({}, this.bindings, { [a]: Object.assign({}, this.bindings[a], { [device]: [code] }) }));\n911:  unbind(a, device) { if (this.rebindable(a)) this._setBindings(Object.assign({}, this.bindings, { [a]: Object.assign({}, this.bindings[a], { [device]: [] }) })); }\n912:  /** forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes */\n914:  _setBindings(b) { if (this._onBindings) this._onBindings(b); else this.bindings = b; }   // (the game saves them in its settings)\n932:   *  'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕' */\n3061:  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\n3079:  if (sp.type === 'bindings') {\n3103:    game.input._settings = this; game.input._onBindings = b => this.set('bindings', b);\n3722: *    unchanged), each other an input of its own, with game.input's API, its device and its bindings: a gamepad each, or\n3738: *  A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action\n3741:  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {},\n9269:class Menu {\n9335:E.Menu = Menu;\n768:    /** clickAt: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y], for the one step after it (clicked()) */\n854:      const d = this._down; this._down = null;   // a click or tap: lifted within a few pixels of where it landed (a drag, the stick's, is none): clicked() for a step,\n1097:   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\n1098:  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\n1106:  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4983f3c-8ab3-4cb5-bbfd-23a240d1dce6","uuid":"5c49aba7-7d8e-4916-bc9d-4de777510109","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:14:07.517Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.89.1: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n```\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module STORY: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * STORY  conversations as data run through a Dialog, flags and values, quests, emote balloons\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { px } = E;\nconst HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RRRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a' });\nGame.prototype._needSync = function () {\n  const fine = window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches, coarse = window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\n  const need = coarse && !fine && !this._keyed && this.input.padIndex === null, el = this._needEl;\n  if (!need) { if (el) el.style.display = 'none'; return; }\n  if (!el) {\n    const d = this._needEl = document.createElement('div'); d.setAttribute('data-sys', 'need'); d.setAttribute('role', 'alert');\n    d.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:24px;text-align:center;background:rgba(5,3,12,.88);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\n    d.innerHTML = '<div><div style=\"font-size:21px;margin-bottom:8px\">Controller or keyboard required</div><div style=\"opacity:.8;margin-bottom:18px\">This game plays with a controller or a keyboard. Connect one, then press any button.</div><button type=\"button\" style=\"font:inherit;padding:10px 22px;border-radius:10px;border:2px solid #b8a8ff;background:#2a2050;color:#fff;min-width:44px;min-height:\n    d.querySelector('button').onclick = () => this.menu('settings');\n    (this.screen.canvas.parentElement || document.body).appendChild(d);\n  }\n  this._needEl.style.display = this.shell && this.shell.screen ? 'none' : 'flex';   // (Settings open over it: hidden while it is)\n};\n/* =============================================================================\n * 11. HUMANOID RIG\n *    Local frame: f = forward, r = right, z = up. The rig poses itself every step\n *    from movement, attacks and state, then projects through any view.\n *    Attack specs (angles relative to facing, + = toward the right hand):\n *      { a0, a1, z0, z1, reach, blade, spin }   e.g. horizontal slash a0: 1.7 -> a1: -1.9\n *    Drive with rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack:{ spec, phase, u } })\n *    where phase is 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover' and u is 0..1 progress in that phase.\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst HUMAN_COLORS = {\n  skin: '#f1c7a0', hair: '#3b2a2f', cloth: '#2f8f86', pants: '#3b3552', boot: '#6a4128', belt: '#e0a84a',\n  cape: '#c8452f', capeIn: '#7a2622', metal: '#dce8f1', metalDk: '#7f93ab', hilt: '#e8b04e', eye: '#1a1320'\n};\nconst JOINT_KEYS = ['hipL', 'hipR', 'kneeL', 'kneeR', 'footL', 'footR', 'hipC', 'shC', 'shL', 'shR', 'head', 'elbowL', 'elbowR', 'handL', 'handR'];\n/** body proportions: 'chibi' (default, big head, Secret of Mana), 'heroic' (tall, Symphony of the Night), 'bulky' (brawlers, bosses) */\nconst BUILDS = {\n792:     *  0..1; the first that holds the finger wins), or null: a pinball's two halves, a rhythm game's lanes. A finger\n807:     *  game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them) */\n863:  /** switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings\n864:   *  (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER,\n869:    const B = this.bindings || {};\n874:      if (!Array.isArray(map[a])) continue;   // (a preset's halves: Input.halfKeys)\n894:  /** the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them) */\n895:  get bindings() { return this._bindings || {}; }\n896:  set bindings(b) { this._bindings = b && typeof b === 'object' ? b : {}; if (this.preset) this.use(this.preset); }\n907:    this._setBindings(Object.assign({}, this.bindings, { [a]: Object.assign({}, this.bindings[a], { [device]: [code] }) }));\n911:  unbind(a, device) { if (this.rebindable(a)) this._setBindings(Object.assign({}, this.bindings, { [a]: Object.assign({}, this.bindings[a], { [device]: [] }) })); }\n912:  /** forget the player's bindings: every action back to its preset's codes */\n914:  _setBindings(b) { if (this._onBindings) this._onBindings(b); else this.bindings = b; }   // (the game saves them in its settings)\n932:   *  'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕' */\n3061:  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\n3079:  if (sp.type === 'bindings') {\n3103:    game.input._settings = this; game.input._onBindings = b => this.set('bindings', b);\n3722: *    unchanged), each other an input of its own, with game.input's API, its device and its bindings: a gamepad each, or\n3738: *  A preset's own halves come first: preset.halves = { left: { pass: ['KeyR'] }, right: { pass: ['KeyL'] } } (an action\n3741:  const P = typeof preset === 'string' ? Input[preset.toUpperCase()] || Input.DEFAULT : preset || Input.DEFAULT, H = KEY_HALVES[side] || KEY_HALVES.left, own = (P.halves && P.halves[side]) || {},\n9269:class Menu {\n9335:E.Menu = Menu;\n768:    /** clickAt: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y], for the one step after it (clicked()) */\n854:      const d = this._down; this._down = null;   // a click or tap: lifted within a few pixels of where it landed (a drag, the stick's, is none): clicked() for a step,\n1097:   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\n1098:  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\n1106:  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VgpSvSn8NLhdoD1hHjFyXk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
