{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017PdshPQgbqhkcTJawKLx7A","type":"tool_result","content":"10:  _hat(g, Sp, J, r, H) {\n11:    const h = this.o.hat, st = h.style || 'cap', c = h.color || '#d83a2a', draw = HUMANOID_HATS[st];\n4496:        cap(A, B, ra, rb, dk);\n4497:        cap(A, B, Math.max(.45, ra - .7), Math.max(.45, rb - .7), base, -.6, -.6);\n4533:      cap(core0, rib1, .32 * u, .32 * u, b.sh); px.line(g, core0[0] - .5, core0[1], rib1[0] - .5, rib1[1], b.base);   // spine below the ribs\n4534:      const pl = Sp(J.hipL, 0, -.2, .9), pr = Sp(J.hipR, 0, .2, .9); cap(pl, pr, .75 * u, .75 * u, b.sh); cap(pl, pr, Math.max(.4, .75 * u - .8), Math.max(.4, .75 * u - .8), b.base, -.5, -.5);\n4536:      cap(rib0, rib1, rw, rb, b.sh); cap(rib0, rib1, Math.max(.5, rw - .9), Math.max(.5, rb - .9), b.base, -.5, -.5);\n676:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color }; E.Humanoid.hat adds one); weapon: 'sword' | 'gun' | 'staff' (E.Humanoid.weapon adds one); hood: true (drawn in colors.hair); dra\n677:- `E.Humanoid.hat(id, draw)` †: a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h.g, h.rig\n678:- `E.Humanoid.hats` †: the hats a Humanoid may wear, by id: the built-ins (cap, band, crown, helmet, pointed) and a game's own\nHumanoid.weapon = (id, spec) => { HUMANOID_WEAPONS[id] = Object.assign({ length: 10, rest: [.55, .35, -.75], blade: true }, spec); return HUMANOID_WEAPONS[id]; };\n/** a hat of the game's own: draw(h) with h.at(forward, right, up) a point round the head on screen, h.r its radius\n *  there, h.c its color (o.hat.color), h.dk a darker one, h.g, h.rig */\nHumanoid.hat = (id, draw) => { HUMANOID_HATS[id] = draw; return draw; };\n/** a held pose of the game's own: fn(J, w, rig) moves the joints (the rig's frame: forward, right, up) toward the pose by\n *  w, 0..1, which eases in and out as state.pose names it or not (blended over the rig's solve) */\nHumanoid.pose = (id, fn) => { HUMANOID_POSES[id] = fn; return fn; };\n\n/**\n4245:    for (const id in HUMANOID_POSES) { const w = OW[id] = approach(OW[id] || 0, s.pose === id ? 1 : 0, dt * 9); if (w > 0) HUMANOID_POSES[id](this.J, w, this); }\n4884:Humanoid.pose = (id, fn) => { HUMANOID_POSES[id] = fn; return fn; };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4983f3c-8ab3-4cb5-bbfd-23a240d1dce6","uuid":"7f2899df-a157-4d9a-a89e-a57081c9abb5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:56:13.344Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"10:  _hat(g, Sp, J, r, H) {\n11:    const h = this.o.hat, st = h.style || 'cap', c = h.color || '#d83a2a', draw = HUMANOID_HATS[st];\n4496:        cap(A, B, ra, rb, dk);\n4497:        cap(A, B, Math.max(.45, ra - .7), Math.max(.45, rb - .7), base, -.6, -.6);\n4533:      cap(core0, rib1, .32 * u, .32 * u, b.sh); px.line(g, core0[0] - .5, core0[1], rib1[0] - .5, rib1[1], b.base);   // spine below the ribs\n4534:      const pl = Sp(J.hipL, 0, -.2, .9), pr = Sp(J.hipR, 0, .2, .9); cap(pl, pr, .75 * u, .75 * u, b.sh); cap(pl, pr, Math.max(.4, .75 * u - .8), Math.max(.4, .75 * u - .8), b.base, -.5, -.5);\n4536:      cap(rib0, rib1, rw, rb, b.sh); cap(rib0, rib1, Math.max(.5, rw - .9), Math.max(.5, rb - .9), b.base, -.5, -.5);\n676:- `new E.Humanoid(o = {}) → rig`: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, build, weapon, outfit, hair, hat, sleeves, armor, hood, cape, colors, ... }): a character rig posed from math every step (API.md, \"Characters\", lists the options); update(dt, state) each step, draw(g, ox, oy, view) inside r.actor. hat: 'cap' | 'band' | 'crown' | 'helmet' | 'pointed' (or { style, color