{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQWw6NLbcbvCdbFs4XN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011tMAL1FDASXTLRspHgC5sG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-061300__x488eb9/work/Sec*-061300/ && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(f,a,b):\n    s=open(f).read(); assert a in s,(f,a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b,1); open(f,'w').write(s)\nsub('src/art/glyphs.js',\"G.promptWidth =\",\"G.drawStick = (g, side, x, y, dir) => { px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 6, 6, '#101820'); px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 6, 5, '#26303a'); const a = dir === undefined ? null : dir / 8 * 6.2832 - 1.5708, kx = a === null ? 0 : Math.cos(a) * 2.5, ky = a === null ? 0 : Math.sin(a) * 2.5; px.disc(g, x + 6 + kx, y + 6 + ky, 3, '#8fb8b0'); font.text(g, side, x + 4 + kx, y + 3 + ky, '#101820', { outline: false, font: 'tiny' }); return 14; };\\nG.promptWidth =\")\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (inp) font.text(g, inp.lastDevice === 'gamepad' ? 'L stick ' + ['↑', '↗', '→', '↘', '↓', '↙', '←', '↖'][num] : 'Key ' + (num + 1), X + 26, Y + 12, '#e8fbf6', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); }\",\"if (inp) { if (inp.lastDevice === 'gamepad') { G.drawStick(g, 'L', X + 26, Y + 10, num); } else font.text(g, 'Key ' + (num + 1), X + 26, Y + 12, '#e8fbf6', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); } }\")\n# tutorial prompt beside the target\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (n) G.ringDraw(g, n.at[0] + OX | 0, n.at[1] + OY | 0, 10 + ((this.t * 4) % 1) * 16, '#ffe08a', 20, 2); }\",\"if (n) { const tx = n.at[0] + OX | 0, ty = n.at[1] + OY | 0; G.ringDraw(g, tx, ty, 10 + ((this.t * 4) % 1) * 16, '#ffe08a', 20, 2); if (inp) { const lab = G.TOOL_NAMES[n.tool], w = font.width(lab) + 26, bx = tx + 18 + w > r.W ? tx - w - 18 : tx + 18; G.panel(g, bx, ty - 12, w, 24, .9); G.toolIcon(g, n.tool, bx + 2, ty - 10, '#ffe08a'); font.text(g, lab, bx + 24, ty - 4, '#ffe08a', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); } } }\")\n# Dev Info: last events\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (e[0] !== 'beat' && e[0] !== 'spawn') this.lastEv = e[0];\",\"if (e[0] !== 'beat' && e[0] !== 'spawn') { this.lastEvs = [e[0], ...(this.lastEvs || [])].slice(0, 4); this.lastEv = this.lastEvs.join(', '); }\")\n# grain chroma\nsub('src/main.js',\"const v = a >>> 24, r = (a >>> 16) & 31, b = (a >>> 8) & 31; E.px.rect(g, x, y, 1, 1, 'rgb(' + (v * .8 + r | 0) + ',' + (v * .9 | 0) + ',' + (v * .8 + b | 0) + ')');\",\"const v = a >>> 24, r = (a >>> 16) & 63, b = (a >>> 8) & 63, q = (a >>> 2) & 31; E.px.rect(g, x, y, 1, 1, 'rgb(' + Math.min(255, v * .7 + r | 0) + ',' + Math.min(255, v * .75 + q | 0) + ',' + Math.min(255, v * .7 + b | 0) + ')');\")\nEOF\necho \"30 second audit pass: stick icon missing, Dev Info showed one event, tutorial prompt not beside the target\" >> notes/feedback.md; sed -i 's/34 issues: 26 from/37 issues: 26 from/; s/and 8 more from a line-by-line audit/and 11 more from line-by-line audits/' src/about-data.json\ncat > notes/plan-audit.md <<'EOF'\n# PLAN.md, section by section, against the final build\nT = a check in tests/run.mjs, B = tests/browser.py, H = tests/hub.py, S = looked at in a screenshot or filmstrip, C = code read. \"Differs\" items are listed at the end.\n\n**0 Use.** Title by real RNG, one constant G.GAME_TITLE (C, H). notes/feedback.md kept (C).\n**1 Pitch and originality.** Forbidden names grepped (T). Pillars: phase checkpoints and offered Intern (T).\n**2 Direction.** overhead op, portraits, threequarter ward, side title (S). res [426,240] expand (B sizes). One self-contained file, no CDN, file:// (B).\n**3 Facts.** Input map keeps base moves; music .1 (T, B); glyph labels (T, B); pad reading (B); Shell tv (B pause rows); touch notice patch (B); session options (H).\n**4 Flow.** Every scene reached: title, menu, difficulty, story, chart, op, lost, results, ward, casefiles, lobby, about, credits, attract, hubround (T playthrough and draw pass, H). First launch to Case 1 with real keys (B).\n**5.1 Table, HUD.** Monitor, clock, objective, speaker, bark, gauge, flow, cursor prompt (S); inside the screen at four sizes (B, S).\n**5.2 Vitals, clock, slips.** Drains, clock loss, slips (T). Five channels: number, ECG, beep, double thump, readouts; CRITICAL text (C, S).\n**5.3 Cursor.** Speed, fine, magnet, guide-follow (T). Mouse 1:1 (B). Keyboard, nudge (T, C). Glove, pointer hidden (B, S). Loupe (C).\n**5.4 Wheel.** Eight directions, keys, flick (T). L1/R1, wheel, Q/E (B). Swap .12 s (T). Hints (C, S).\n**5.5 Eight tools.** Each right gesture and each wrong one (T).\n**5.6 Grades, Flow, ranks.** (T). Four tiles, stamp (S).\n**5.7 Gifts.** Long Breath, Second Look exact restore and ghosts, Consult (T). Cold palette, tracking lines (S).\n**5.8 Code Blue.** Timing, revive, loss, none on Attending (T). Paddles, marker on the peak (S).\n**5.9 Closing.** Ring, stamp, chord (T via playthrough, S).\n**5.10 Failing.** Checkpoint, cap at B, Intern after two failures, tutorial freeze (T). Targets (T, tools/slow.mjs).\n**5.11 Feel table.** Every row has its sound, picture and rumble in OpView.present (C). Blood color setting (C).\n**6 Controls.** Bindings as listed (C). Prompts by device; stick icon (T, B, C). Swap sticks (C).\n**7 Objects.** Every type in the story (T). Hidden, under pool (T). Phase scripts as data (T validator).\n**8 Strains.** Staccato, Legato including snap, Tremolo, Da Capo including repeat, Fermata domes, Cantor's four movements and forced rewind (T).\n**9 Cases.** All eleven play in order (T). Lightbox in Cases 2, 4, 10 (C, S). Skills Lab by unlocks (T). Grand Rounds (T).\n**10 Story.** All beats written in src/data/story; 215 lines; line length, speakers, expressions, reachable nodes (T). Barks: shared pool, per case (T).\n**11 Ward.** Two maps, people by chapter, hover and click (C, S), autosave (T), morale (C), door within 8 tiles (C).\n**12 Grand Rounds.** Scales by N, 1 to 4 bots, retractor solo and two (T). Couch join (T). Hub: four runs, client stroke, standalone (H). Awards, standings (S, C).\n**13 Attract.** 10 s on title, menu, casefiles, lobby (T, C); exits by key, mouse, click, stick, pad (T, B); loops twice; never saves (T); on phones (B).\n**14 Dev.** Four tabs (T). Every slider has a behavior test, Reset (T). Cheats (T). Jump, spawn (T). Info, Copy (C). DEV tag, no rank saved (C). Hidden in sessions (C).\n**15 UI.** Focus and hover (B, C). Settings list (C). Case Files one folder at a time (S). About sections (B).\n**16 Art.** Seven sites, ten stages, cast of sixteen busts, instruments, tiles, title, lightbox (S). Hospital shapes as data (C).\n**17 Animation.** Poses and cinematics (S filmstrips). Field and strains procedural (S).\n**18 Audio.** Effects, voices, choir not silent; music below effects (B). No audio files (C). Mix defaults (T).\n**19 Architecture.** Sim plain data, deterministic (T). Content as data, CONTENT.md (T, C).\n**20 Testing.** One command; all listed groups present (T, B, H). check.mjs and filmstrip.mjs run (S).\n**21 Build order.** Reached M9.\n**22 Done checklist.** notes/checklist.md.\n\n## Differs from the plan, on purpose\n- Section 9's clocks and counts are raised in most cases (extra.js). Section 9 says they are defaults to balance. Cases 1 to 10 now take a first-timer 3.1 to 4.1 minutes.\n- Case 11 takes that first-timer 5.9 minutes. Its fixed content (four movements, six repeat cycles at about 17 s each) and its clock of 420 s plus 120 s a movement are the plan's own.\n- Staccato bite damage, Tremolo miss damage and Da Capo's growing window are tuned from bot runs (section 5.10: \"tune its numbers\").\n- Section 19's file list is partly merged; the dithering is softer than Appendix A.\n\n## Not possible on this computer (TASK.md: \"never required\")\nA person's hands, a physical controller, someone listening, a real iPhone or iPad, a TV. Stand-ins used as TASK.md directs.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs; cat > notes/rf.sh <<'EOF'\nwait_mem(){ n=0; while [ \"$(awk '/MemAvailable/{print int($2/1048576)}' /proc/meminfo)\" -lt 4 ] && [ $n -lt 60 ]; do sleep 15; n=$((n+1)); done; }\nwait_mem; npm install --silent --no-audit --no-fund playwright@1.63.0 >/dev/null 2>&1; H=$(cd .. && pwd)/SecondScalpel-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-061300.html\nfor s in \"\" \"#about\" \"#credits\" \"#chart-c2\" \"#difficulty\" \"#lobby\" \"#casefiles\" \"#story-c7_after\" \"#story-c8_before\" \"#ward-ward3-3\" \"#ward-ship-7\" \"#op-c1-0\" \"#op-c11-2\"; do wait_mem; echo \"$s: $(timeout 100 node vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/tools/check.mjs \"$H$s\" --seconds 2 --out notes/check 2>&1 | grep -E 'load |^    |no errors|rror' | sed -E 's/.*(scene [a-z]+).*(filled +[0-9]+ colors).*/\\2/; s/  +/ /g' | grep -vE '\"view ' | cut -c1-100 | tr '\\n' ';')\"; done; rm -rf notes/check node_modules package-lock.json\nfor i in 1 2; do wait_mem; echo \"full run $i\"; node tests/run.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v \"^my-3D2dge\" | cut -c1-400 | tail -6 > notes/lr.txt; cat notes/lr.txt; grep -q \" 0 failed\" notes/lr.txt && break; done; rm -rf tests/hubdir notes/lr.txt; sha1sum ../*.html | cut -c1-12\nEOF\nbash notes/rf.sh; rm -f notes/rf.sh","description":"Fix audit misses, write full audit, rebuild, verify everything","timeout":5400000,"run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3305,"cache_read_input_tokens":703488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3305},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4983f3c-8ab3-4cb5-bbfd-23a240d1dce6","uuid":"74dd12ee-5424-4c99-890a-ec1108c5dce7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T20:24:54.469Z","request_id":"req_011CgkQWviJG51W3rWYB4WA8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011tMAL1FDASXTLRspHgC5sG":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-061300__x488eb9/work/Sec*-061300/ && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(f,a,b):\n    s=open(f).read(); assert a in s,(f,a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b,1); open(f,'w').write(s)\nsub('src/art/glyphs.js',\"G.promptWidth =\",\"G.drawStick = (g, side, x, y, dir) => { px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 6, 6, '#101820'); px.disc(g, x + 6, y + 6, 5, '#26303a'); const a = dir === undefined ? null : dir / 8 * 6.2832 - 1.5708, kx = a === null ? 0 : Math.cos(a) * 2.5, ky = a === null ? 0 : Math.sin(a) * 2.5; px.disc(g, x + 6 + kx, y + 6 + ky, 3, '#8fb8b0'); font.text(g, side, x + 4 + kx, y + 3 + ky, '#101820', { outline: false, font: 'tiny' }); return 14; };\\nG.promptWidth =\")\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (inp) font.text(g, inp.lastDevice === 'gamepad' ? 'L stick ' + ['↑', '↗', '→', '↘', '↓', '↙', '←', '↖'][num] : 'Key ' + (num + 1), X + 26, Y + 12, '#e8fbf6', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); }\",\"if (inp) { if (inp.lastDevice === 'gamepad') { G.drawStick(g, 'L', X + 26, Y + 10, num); } else font.text(g, 'Key ' + (num + 1), X + 26, Y + 12, '#e8fbf6', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); } }\")\n# tutorial prompt beside the target\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (n) G.ringDraw(g, n.at[0] + OX | 0, n.at[1] + OY | 0, 10 + ((this.t * 4) % 1) * 16, '#ffe08a', 20, 2); }\",\"if (n) { const tx = n.at[0] + OX | 0, ty = n.at[1] + OY | 0; G.ringDraw(g, tx, ty, 10 + ((this.t * 4) % 1) * 16, '#ffe08a', 20, 2); if (inp) { const lab = G.TOOL_NAMES[n.tool], w = font.width(lab) + 26, bx = tx + 18 + w > r.W ? tx - w - 18 : tx + 18; G.panel(g, bx, ty - 12, w, 24, .9); G.toolIcon(g, n.tool, bx + 2, ty - 10, '#ffe08a'); font.text(g, lab, bx + 24, ty - 4, '#ffe08a', { outline: false, shadow: '#000' }); } } }\")\n# Dev Info: last events\nsub('src/scenes/op.js',\"if (e[0] !== 'beat' && e[0] !== 'spawn') this.lastEv = e[0];\",\"if (e[0] !== 'beat' && e[0] !== 'spawn') { this.lastEvs = [e[0], ...(this.lastEvs || [])].slice(0, 4); this.lastEv = this.lastEvs.join(', '); }\")\n# grain chroma\nsub('src/main.js',\"const v = a >>> 24, r = (a >>> 16) & 31, b = (a >>> 8) & 31; E.px.rect(g, x, y, 1, 1, 'rgb(' + (v * .8 + r | 0) + ',' + (v * .9 | 0) + ',' + (v * .8 + b | 0) + ')');\",\"const v = a >>> 24, r = (a >>> 16) & 63, b = (a >>> 8) & 63, q = (a >>> 2) & 31; E.px.rect(g, x, y, 1, 1, 'rgb(' + Math.min(255, v * .7 + r | 0) + ',' + Math.min(255, v * .75 + q | 0) + ',' + Math.min(255, v * .7 + b | 0) + ')');\")\nEOF\necho \"30 second audit pass: stick icon missing, Dev Info showed one event, tutorial prompt not beside the target\" >> notes/feedback.md; sed -i 's/34 issues: 26 from/37 issues: 26 from/; s/and 8 more from a line-by-line audit/and 11 more from line-by-line audits/' src/about-data.json\ncat > notes/plan-audit.md <<'EOF'\n# PLAN.md, section by section, against the final build\nT = a check in tests/run.mjs, B = tests/browser.py, H = tests/hub.py, S = looked at in a screenshot or filmstrip, C = code read. \"Differs\" items are listed at the end.\n\n**0 Use.** Title by real RNG, one constant G.GAME_TITLE (C, H). notes/feedback.md kept (C).\n**1 Pitch and originality.** Forbidden names grepped (T). Pillars: phase checkpoints and offered Intern (T).\n**2 Direction.** overhead op, portraits, threequarter ward, side title (S). res [426,240] expand (B sizes). One self-contained file, no CDN, file:// (B).\n**3 Facts.** Input map keeps base moves; music .1 (T, B); glyph labels (T, B); pad reading (B); Shell tv (B pause rows); touch notice patch (B); session options (H).\n**4 Flow.** Every scene reached: title, menu, difficulty, story, chart, op, lost, results, ward, casefiles, lobby, about, credits, attract, hubround (T playthrough and draw pass, H). First launch to Case 1 with real keys (B).\n**5.1 Table, HUD.** Monitor, clock, objective, speaker, bark, gauge, flow, cursor prompt (S); inside the screen at four sizes (B, S).\n**5.2 Vitals, clock, slips.** Drains, clock loss, slips (T). Five channels: number, ECG, beep, double thump, readouts; CRITICAL text (C, S).\n**5.3 Cursor.** Speed, fine, magnet, guide-follow (T). Mouse 1:1 (B). Keyboard, nudge (T, C). Glove, pointer hidden (B, S). Loupe (C).\n**5.4 Wheel.** Eight directions, keys, flick (T). L1/R1, wheel, Q/E (B). Swap .12 s (T). Hints (C, S).\n**5.5 Eight tools.** Each right gesture and each wrong one (T).\n**5.6 Grades, Flow, ranks.** (T). Four tiles, stamp (S).\n**5.7 Gifts.** Long Breath, Second Look exact restore and ghosts, Consult (T). Cold palette, tracking lines (S).\n**5.8 Code Blue.** Timing, revive, loss, none on Attending (T). Paddles, marker on the peak (S).\n**5.9 Closing.** Ring, stamp, chord (T via playthrough, S).\n**5.10 Failing.** Checkpoint, cap at B, Intern after two failures, tutorial freeze (T). Targets (T, tools/slow.mjs).\n**5.11 Feel table.** Every row has its sound, picture and rumble in OpView.present (C). Blood color setting (C).\n**6 Controls.** Bindings as listed (C). Prompts by device; stick icon (T, B, C). Swap sticks (C).\n**7 Objects.** Every type in the story (T). Hidden, under pool (T). Phase scripts as data (T validator).\n**8 Strains.** Staccato, Legato including snap, Tremolo, Da Capo including repeat, Fermata domes, Cantor's four movements and forced rewind (T).\n**9 Cases.** All eleven play in order (T). Lightbox in Cases 2, 4, 10 (C, S). Skills Lab by unlocks (T). Grand Rounds (T).\n**10 Story.** All beats written in src/data/story; 215 lines; line length, speakers, expressions, reachable nodes (T). Barks: shared pool, per case (T).\n**11 Ward.** Two maps, people by chapter, hover and click (C, S), autosave (T), morale (C), door within 8 tiles (C).\n**12 Grand Rounds.** Scales by N, 1 to 4 bots, retractor solo and two (T). Couch join (T). Hub: four runs, client stroke, standalone (H). Awards, standings (S, C).\n**13 Attract.** 10 s on title, menu, casefiles, lobby (T, C); exits by key, mouse, click, stick, pad (T, B); loops twice; never saves (T); on phones (B).\n**14 Dev.** Four tabs (T). Every slider has a behavior test, Reset (T). Cheats (T). Jump, spawn (T). Info, Copy (C). DEV tag, no rank saved (C). Hidden in sessions (C).\n**15 UI.** Focus and hover (B, C). Settings list (C). Case Files one folder at a time (S). About sections (B).\n**16 Art.** Seven sites, ten stages, cast of sixteen busts, instruments, tiles, title, lightbox (S). Hospital shapes as data (C).\n**17 Animation.** Poses and cinematics (S filmstrips). Field and strains procedural (S).\n**18 Audio.** Effects, voices, choir not silent; music below effects (B). No audio files (C). Mix defaults (T).\n**19 Architecture.** Sim plain data, deterministic (T). Content as data, CONTENT.md (T, C).\n**20 Testing.** One command; all listed groups present (T, B, H). check.mjs and filmstrip.mjs run (S).\n**21 Build order.** Reached M9.\n**22 Done checklist.** notes/checklist.md.\n\n## Differs from the plan, on purpose\n- Section 9's clocks and counts are raised in most cases (extra.js). Section 9 says they are defaults to balance. Cases 1 to 10 now take a first-timer 3.1 to 4.1 minutes.\n- Case 11 takes that first-timer 5.9 minutes. Its fixed content (four movements, six repeat cycles at about 17 s each) and its clock of 420 s plus 120 s a movement are the plan's own.\n- Staccato bite damage, Tremolo miss damage and Da Capo's growing window are tuned from bot runs (section 5.10: \"tune its numbers\").\n- Section 19's file list is partly merged; the dithering is softer than Appendix A.\n\n## Not possible on this computer (TASK.md: \"never required\")\nA person's hands, a physical controller, someone listening, a real iPhone or iPad, a TV. Stand-ins used as TASK.md directs.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs; cat > notes/rf.sh <<'EOF'\nwait_mem(){ n=0; while [ \"$(awk '/MemAvailable/{print int($2/1048576)}' /proc/meminfo)\" -lt 4 ] && [ $n -lt 60 ]; do sleep 15; n=$((n+1)); done; }\nwait_mem; npm install --silent --no-audit --no-fund playwright@1.63.0 >/dev/null 2>&1; H=$(cd .. 